# CVE-2026-85091 (zlib, in cgr.dev/chainguard/wolfi-base): Trivy's DB lists
# the fix as 1.3.3-r0, but as of 2026-09-16 the Wolfi apk repo does not carry
# it yet -- the newest build there is zlib-1.3.2.1_rc20260601-r0, confirmed
# with `docker run --rm cgr.dev/chainguard/wolfi-base:latest apk list -a zlib`.
# `apk upgrade --no-cache zlib` in Dockerfile.adapter-with-plugins is left in
# place so the fixed build is picked up the moment Chainguard publishes it --
# remove this line at that point, not before.
CVE-2026-85091

# GO-2026-5932 (golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp): a deprecation notice, not a bug
# -- the openpgp package is unmaintained and will never get a fix version, so
# every x/crypto release is flagged. We do not import openpgp (`go list -deps
# ./...` shows only x/crypto/blake2b and pbkdf2). x/crypto itself stays: blake2b
# is the Beckn signing hash (signer.go, signvalidator.go), and grpc, x/net,
# opa, jwx and vault require the module anyway. Remove this line if anything
# here starts importing x/crypto/openpgp.
GO-2026-5932
